romanized_response:
HTTP status code 429 Too Many Requests ante server ki oka rate limit undani, mee request aa limit ni daatindani artham. Idi kindi kaaranala valla jarigi undochu:

1. Ee request chese code ni chala takkuva samayam lo chala sarlu run cheyadam valla rate limit daatindi.

2. Website spam ani anumaninche requests ni 429 status code tho reject chestundi. Ante mee user agent oka common browser kaadu ani artham, idi konni websites chese oka simple check. Dini sari cheyadaaniki, meeru GET request ki "User-Agent" header ni ila add cheyochu:

```
const response = await axios.get('https://www.realestate.com.au/rent/in-sydney,+nsw/list-1', 
     { headers: { 'User-Agent': 'browser.version' }  }
);
```

"browser.version" ni oka real browser user agent string tho replace cheyalsi untundi ani gurtinchandi. Ee code run avtunna application ni batti, idi user agent spoofing ga pariganinchabadochu, adi konni deshalu leda organizations (leda aa website terms of service) chattam prakaram restricted avochu.

3. Website vere edaina kaaranam valla requests ni rate limit chestundi. Idi oka proxy dwara request cheyadam valla avochu, ala aithe proxy ni use chese itara users chala requests chesi undochu, kani idi takkuva sambhavam.

4. Website denial of service attack lo undadam valla anni requests ni reject chestundi. Idi takkuva sambhavam, endukante alanti attack lo unna server yokka typical behavior traffic ni leni server ki route cheyadam, leda daani purtiga deny cheyadam, emi valid response ivvadam. Kaani, website HTTP status code tho respond chesina, adi server overload ayinappudu icche 503 Service Unavailable avochu.

response_en:
Yes, certainly! The issue you're encountering is because the string literals "fizzbuzz", "fizz", and "buzz" are temporary values, and you are trying to return a reference to them, which is not allowed because they will be dropped at the end of the scope, and the returned reference would be dangling.

You can fix this error by returning &'static str instead of &str. &'static str refers to string literals, which have a 'static lifetime, meaning they last for the duration of the program. Here's an updated version of your code:

fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) -> &'static str {
    match (n % 3, n % 5) {
        (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",
        (0, _) => "fizz",
        (_, 0) => "buzz",
        _ => {
            let s = n.to_string();
            Box::leak(s.into_boxed_str())
        }
    }
}

Note that the last arm returns a &'static str that is created from a String using the Box::leak function, which takes ownership of a Box<T> and returns a pointer to its contents, effectively leaking it. This is safe because the returned pointer will last for the duration of the program, but it should be used with care as it will not be cleaned up automatically.

romanized_response:
Avunu, tappakunda! Meeru ఎదుర్కొంటున్న issue enti ante, "fizzbuzz", "fizz", mariyu "buzz" ane string literals temporary values, mariyu meeru vatiki oka reference ni return cheyadaaniki prayatnistunnaru. Idi allow cheyaru endukante avi scope mugisina ventane drop avutaayi, appudu return chesina reference dangling avtundi.

Ee error ni fix cheyadaaniki, meeru &str badulu &'static str ni return cheyochu. &'static str string literals ni refer chestundi, vatiki 'static lifetime untundi, ante avi program duration antha untaayi ani ardham. Ikkada mee code ki update chesina version undi:

fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) -> &'static str {
    match (n % 3, n % 5) {
        (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",
        (0, _) => "fizz",
        (_, 0) => "buzz",
        _ => {
            let s = n.to_string();
            Box::leak(s.into_boxed_str())
        }
    }
}

Chudandi, chivari arm oka &'static str ni return chestundi, adi Box::leak function ni use chesi oka String nunchi create cheyabaddadi. Box::leak oka Box<T> ki ownership teesukuni, daani contents ki oka pointer ni return chestundi, effectively daanni leak chestundi. Idi safe, endukante return chesina pointer program duration antha untundi, kaani deenni jagrattaga vaadali, endukante adi automatically clean up avvadu.

response_en:
Merge sort is a divide and conquer algorithm that works by recursively splitting the input array in half until the arrays are split into single elements. Then, the sorted arrays are merged back together in sorted order.

The key benefits of merge sort over a simpler algorithm like bubble sort are:

1. It is a stable sort that does not change the relative order of elements with equal keys.
2. It has an efficiency of O(n log n) time complexity, making it a relatively efficient algorithm even for large input sizes. Bubble sort, on the other hand, has a quadratic time complexity of O(n^2), making it very inefficient for larger inputs.
3. It is a generic algorithm that can sort any type of data for which a comparison function exists.

Here is a Rust implementation example:
```rust
fn merge_sort(vec: &mut [i32]) {
    if vec.len() < 2 {
        return;
    }

    let mid = vec.len() / 2;
    let (left, right) = vec.split_at_mut(mid);

    merge_sort(left);
    merge_sort(right);

    merge(left, right, vec);
}

fn merge(left: &mut [i32], right: &mut [i32], vec: &mut [i32]) {
    let mut i = 0;
    let mut j = 0;
    let mut k = 0;

    while i < left.len() && j < right.len() {
        if left[i] < right[j] {
            vec[k] = left[i];
            i += 1;
        } else {
            vec[k] = right[j];
            j += 1;
        }
        k += 1;
    }

    while i < left.len() {
        vec[k] = left[i];
        i += 1;
        k += 1;
    }

    while j < right.len() {
        vec[k] = right[j];
        j += 1;
        k += 1;
    }
}
```

romanized_response:
Merge sort anedi oka divide and conquer algorithm. Idi input array ni recursive ga sagam sagam ga split chestu, prathi array single elements ga split ayye varaku pani chestundi. Tarvatha, sorted arrays ni malli kalipi, sorted order lo merge chestundi.

Bubble sort laanti simple algorithm tho polisthe merge sort yokka mukhyamaina benefits enti ante:

1. Idi oka stable sort. Same keys unna elements yokka relative order ni idi marchadu.
2. Daani efficiency O(n log n) time complexity tho untundi. Idi pedda input sizes ki kuda relatively efficient algorithm ga chestundi. Bubble sort aithe, O(n^2) anedi quadratic time complexity, adi pedda inputs ki chala inefficient ga untundi.
3. Idi oka generic algorithm. Comparison function unna ye type data ni aina idi sort cheyagaladu.

Ikkada oka Rust implementation example undi:
```rust
